key "wang1988"
literal "false"

\end_inset
 shows 
\begin_inset Formula $E_{sp}$
\end_inset
 of the Figure 3 streamer before and after a short drift. That streamer belongs to an impulse of 
\begin_inset Formula $320\,\text{kV}$
\end_inset
 with a time to crest of 
\begin_inset Formula $130\,\mu\text{s}$
\end_inset
 in the 
\begin_inset Formula $80\,\text{cm}$
\end_inset
 gap. Here the first burst of this impulse is computed with the model, not imposed: the time-lag law predicts its inception voltage, the head condition its length and Gauss's law its charge (
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand formatted
reference "tab:repro_fig4_case"
plural "false"
caps "false"
noprefix "false"
nolink "false"
tuple "list"

\end_inset
). The paper does not say how long the drift lasted; in its figure the minimum of the drifted curve, where the apex of the moved cloud sits, is at about 
\begin_inset Formula $0.07\,\text{cm}$
\end_inset
, so the cloud was moved by this distance.
