\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Newpage pagebreak
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Why B and C Are Inputs 
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "sec:app_bc"

\end_inset

\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The paper describes the field in the streamer region as being about 
\begin_inset Formula $E_{c}$
\end_inset
. A natural idea is therefore to find the shape constants from this condition: choose 
\begin_inset Formula $A$
\end_inset
, 
\begin_inset Formula $B$
\end_inset
 and 
\begin_inset Formula $C$
\end_inset
 so that the total field along the first streamer stays as close as possible to 
\begin_inset Formula $E_{c}$
\end_inset
, and let the length follow. This was tried with the scripts wh_calibration.py and solver/calibration.py, which are kept as optional tools.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The space-charge fields are linear in 
